From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] libopenbios: ofmem: keep the upper bits of physical addresses in
 align_ptr()

align_ptr() takes the alignment as a size_t, which is 32 bits wide in
OpenBIOS (include/config.h), and masks the address with ~(a - 1). That
mask is zero-extended to the 64-bit phys_addr_t, so every bit above
bit 31 of the address is cleared.

ofmem_posix_memalign() aligns the physical address of its next block
with align_ptr() and turns it back into a virtual one with pa2va(). On
sparc64 the firmware's .data and .bss (the heap among them) sit at the
top of RAM, so with more than 4 GB of RAM their physical address is
above 4 GB. pa2va() does not recognise the truncated address as one of
the firmware's and returns it unchanged, and the very first malloc()
in ofmem_init() goes wrong before the banner is printed:

  qemu-system-sparc64 -M sun4u -m 4352 (5120, 6144, 7168 the same):
    Unhandled Exception 0x0000000000000030
    PC = 0x00000000ffd15030   (in ofmem_posix_memalign)

  qemu-system-sparc64 -M sun4u -m 8192:
    out of malloc memory (28)!
    Unhandled Exception 0x0000000000000030

Widen the mask to phys_addr_t and take the address as one too.
---
 libopenbios/ofmem_common.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c b/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
index e86eefd..194db15 100644
--- a/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
+++ b/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
@@ -33,9 +33,11 @@ static inline size_t align_size(size_t x, size_t a)
     return (x + a - 1) & ~(a - 1);
 }
 
-static inline phys_addr_t align_ptr(uintptr_t x, size_t a)
+static inline phys_addr_t align_ptr(phys_addr_t x, size_t a)
 {
-    return (x + a - 1) & ~(a - 1);
+    /* size_t is 32 bits wide: widen the mask, or a physical address
+       above 4 GB (sparc64 with more RAM than that) loses its upper bits */
+    return (x + a - 1) & ~((phys_addr_t)a - 1);
 }
 
 static ucell get_ram_size( void )
